      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 23, \"total_count\": 23, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created listing \\\"Upcycled Bicycle Planter\\\" with 2 sample photos, description, price $85, category Home Decor, condition Like New, location Denver CO, and Upcycled Item toggled on. Toast \\\"Listing created successfully!\\\" shown. Product detail page displays all submitted info correctly: title, $85, Home Decor/Like New badges, Denver CO, Upcycled badge, description, 2 photos with nav arrows, seller Sam Seller.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit functionality exists for listings\", \"actual\": \"On My Listings, each owned listing only exposes View, Mark Sold, and Delete actions — no Edit control. The product detail page for an owned listing only shows a \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" button, no edit option. Attempting to navigate directly to /edit-listing/{id} returns a 404 \\\"Page not found\\\". There is no way to edit title, description, photos, price, category, condition, location, or upcycled status of an existing listing.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked Mark Sold on owned listing \\\"Vintage Tin Sign Wall Art\\\": toast \\\"Item marked as sold\\\" shown, status badge changed Active->Sold, button changed to \\\"Mark Available\\\". Clicked Mark Available: toast \\\"Item marked as available\\\" shown, status reverted to Active. Clicked Delete: confirmation alertdialog \\\"Delete listing? This action cannot be undone.\\\" appeared with Cancel/Delete buttons. Confirmed Delete: toast \\\"Listing deleted\\\" shown, listing removed from My Listings (empty state \\\"No listings yet\\\" shown).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As seller Riley Vendor, listing \\\"Reclaimed Wood Coffee Table\\\" was visible in Browse All Items (11 items available) while Active. After clicking \\\"Mark Sold\\\" on My Listings, returned to Browse: item count dropped to \\\"10 items available\\\" and \\\"Reclaimed Wood Coffee Table\\\" no longer appeared in the results grid, confirming sold listings are excluded from buyer browse results.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered timothee.qa.test@example.com with name, password, location; toast \\\"Account created successfully!\\\" shown; header switched to signed-in state showing user name \\\"Timothee Test\\\", Sell button, cart icon.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Applied combined filters: category=Furniture, Upcycled items only, condition=New. Result narrowed correctly from 10 to 3 (Furniture) then to 2 (Furniture+Upcycled+New): \\\"Upcycled Pallet Coffee Table\\\" ($175) and \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\" ($320) - both verified Furniture/Upcycled/New, correctly excluding \\\"Mid-Century Modern Armchair\\\" (Like New, not New). Changed sort to \\\"Price: Low to High\\\" while filters active: order updated to $175 then $320, filters remained applied (still 2 items, both satisfying all 3 criteria).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searched \\\"wood\\\" (lowercase) in Browse search box: results updated instantly to 3 items - \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\" (title match), \\\"Mid-Century Modern Armchair\\\" (description match, likely \\\"wood\\\" in description), \\\"Kids Wooden Train Set\\\" (title match \\\"Wooden\\\") - confirming case-insensitive matching across title/description despite capitalized \\\"Wood\\\"/\\\"Wooden\\\" in source data. Clearing the search box restored full 10-item result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As signed-in buyer Jordan Buyer, clicked \\\"Add to Cart\\\" on \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\" (owned by James Wilson, $320, available). Cart page shows 1 item with correct title \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\", photo thumbnail, location \\\"Portland, OR\\\", price \\\"$320\\\", and Total \\\"$320.00\\\" matching the listing price exactly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As signed-in buyer Jordan Buyer, clicked \\\"Message Seller\\\" on \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\" (owned by James Wilson, available, not own listing). Dialog \\\"Send a message to James Wilson\\\" opened; typed non-empty message \\\"Hi, is this still available? I'd love to pick it up this weekend.\\\" which enabled the previously-disabled \\\"Send Message\\\" button. Clicking it produced toast \\\"Message sent to seller!\\\" confirming submission.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category selection from Categories page does not filter Browse results\", \"actual\": \"On /categories page, \\\"Home Decor\\\" showed \\\"3 items\\\". Clicking it navigated to /?category=home-decor (URL query param correctly set), but the Browse page displayed \\\"11 items available\\\" showing the full unfiltered grid (all 11 listings across all categories, e.g. Yoga Mat & Blocks Set (Sports), Vintage Denim Jacket (Clothing), Sony Headphones (Electronics), Kids Wooden Train Set (Toys), etc.), and the \\\"Home Decor\\\" checkbox in the Categories filter sidebar was not checked/active. Expected: only the 3 Home Decor category listings should be shown with a matching count, per the category page's own stated count.\", \"evidence\": \"URL after click: /?category=home-decor; page still showed \\\"11 items available\\\" and all 11 product cards spanning every category, not just Home Decor.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Seller cannot view buyer's purchase request or message anywhere in the UI\", \"actual\": \"As buyer Blake Buyer, added seller Sasha Seller's listing \\\"QA Test Vase FT22\\\" to cart, sent a message via Message Seller (\\\"Message sent to seller!\\\" confirmed), and clicked \\\"Send Purchase Request\\\" in cart (toast \\\"Purchase requests sent to sellers!\\\" shown, cart cleared to 0 items). Logged out and logged back in as Sasha Seller (the listing owner). Checked: (1) the notification/bell icon in header - clicking it produced no dropdown/panel, just navigated to home with no visible change; (2) user menu - only contains \\\"My Profile\\\" and \\\"My Listings\\\", no Messages/Requests/Notifications option; (3) My Listings page - the listing still shows plain \\\"Active\\\" status with only View/Mark Sold/Delete actions, no indicator of a pending purchase request or unread message; (4) the listing's own detail page (as owner) - only shows \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" button, no request/message content or badge anywhere. There is no UI surface in the application where a seller can see that a purchase request was submitted or read the buyer's message.\", \"evidence\": \"Cart correctly reported \\\"Purchase requests sent to sellers!\\\" only after clicking Send Purchase Request (cart item recorded). However, seller-side visibility of that request/message is completely absent from My Listings, product detail (owner view), notification icon, and user menu.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Logging in with unregistered email nonexistent.user.qa@example.com showed toast \\\"Invalid credentials. Try: emma@example.com\\\"; remained on /login page, not authenticated.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registering with EMMA@example.com (case-variant of existing demo account emma@example.com) was rejected with toast \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\"; no new account was created and form fields were preserved unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password is accepted, granting a signed-in session\", \"actual\": \"Registered account casey.pwtest.qa@example.com with password \\\"correctpass1\\\". Logging in with the same email but an incorrect password \\\"wrongpassword\\\" was accepted: toast \\\"Welcome back!\\\" appeared and the header showed the user as signed in (\\\"Casey Password\\\"), instead of being rejected.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Logged in as Riley Vendor, viewed listing \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\" owned by seller James Wilson (not the current user). Product page shows only \\\"Add to Cart\\\" and \\\"Message Seller\\\" buttons — no Mark Sold, Delete, Edit, or \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" controls are exposed for another user's listing.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing required fields not identified to seller\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the Create Listing form completely empty (no photo, title, description, price, category, condition, location) did not create a listing (correct), but no error message, inline field highlighting, or toast was shown anywhere identifying which fields were missing. Only the Title field silently received focus.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Non-numeric price accepted and listing created with invalid price\", \"actual\": \"Negative price (-25) was correctly rejected (no listing created, stayed on form). However, submitting a non-numeric price value (\\\"abc\\\" in the price field) was accepted: the app navigated to My Listings with toast \\\"Listing created successfully!\\\" and the new listing \\\"QA Test Chair 2\\\" was created and displayed with price \\\"$NaN\\\" instead of being rejected.\", \"evidence\": \"My Listings shows \\\"QA Test Chair 2\\\" with price \\\"$NaN\\\" and status Active after submitting a non-numeric price.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Direct navigation to protected routes while unauthenticated shows a blank page instead of a redirect or sign-in prompt\", \"actual\": \"In-app interactive actions correctly guard authentication: clicking \\\"Add to Cart\\\" on a product detail page while logged out shows toast \\\"Please log in to add items to your cart\\\" and redirects to /login (good); clicking \\\"Message Seller\\\" while logged out shows the message dialog but properly restricted per earlier testing. However, directly navigating (full page load) to protected routes while unauthenticated produces a completely blank page with no content, no redirect to /login, and no sign-in prompt: /create-listing renders blank, /cart renders blank, /my-listings renders blank. Only the notification region divs are present in the DOM; the entire app shell (header, content) fails to render, giving the user no indication of why the page is empty or how to sign in.\", \"evidence\": \"Snapshot for http://localhost:6023/create-listing, /cart, and /my-listings (all accessed unauthenticated via direct navigation) each returned only: generic [active]: generic: region \\\\\\\"Notifications (F8)\\\\\\\": list, region \\\\\\\"Notifications alt+T\\\\\\\" — no banner, no content, no redirect.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Immediately after submitting duplicate email registration, a toast notification \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\" appeared and the registration form remained visible and populated with entered data for correction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"wood\\\" into search box immediately updated result count from \\\"10 items available\\\" to \\\"3 items available\\\" and the grid content, with no separate submit/search button click required. Clearing the box immediately restored \\\"10 items available\\\" and the full grid.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each filter checkbox click (Furniture, Upcycled, New) immediately updated the displayed count and grid without a submit action (10->3->3->2 items). Selecting \\\"Price: Low to High\\\" sort immediately reordered results. Clicking \\\"Clear all filters\\\" immediately restored all 10 items to the grid.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"Add to Cart\\\" on product detail page immediately showed toast \\\"Added to cart!\\\" and the header cart icon immediately updated to show badge \\\"1\\\", without any page reload. Navigating to cart (SPA) showed the item, count \\\"1 item\\\", and correct total, confirming immediate state update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Listing detail page consistently displays all required fields: photo(s) (with nav arrows for multi-photo listings per FT-1), title (heading), description, price, category badge, condition badge, location (with icon), seller name+location, listing date (\\\"Listed 2026-08-24\\\"), and Upcycled badge when applicable (confirmed on multiple items e.g. \\\"Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf\\\", \\\"Upcycled Pallet Coffee Table\\\"). Availability status: verified on a listing marked Sold (\\\"QA Test Vase FT22\\\") - the detail page explicitly shows \\\"This item is no longer available\\\" message beneath the Manage Your Listings button, and the Add to Cart/Message Seller buttons are absent for sold items. All fields confirmed present and consistent across own-active-listing, other-seller-listing, and sold-listing detail page views.\"}]}"
